  "question": {
    "text": "The angle of elevation of the top <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> of a vertical tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;of height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> on the horizontal ground is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be a point on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;and from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, vertically above <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, the angle of elevation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;and the area of the trapezium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>, then the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is"
